{"title":"Pentagon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>, a <b>pentagon</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a> with 5 sides. Each <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polygon\" title=\"Regular polygon\"> regular</a> pentagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8060e5b4b3905a244e7bdb17ac8b6a92a3071b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. The sum of the internal angles of any pentagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9eee47747ea9ac6402d43c061d5a5f95e83327d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Area\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Area</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Construction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Construction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#The_Golden_Ratio\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Golden Ratio</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Area\">Area</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Area\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of a regular pentagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3eec6800b4b37ac502120005a8ed2862f2526a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4}s^2\\sqrt{5(5+2\\sqrt{5})}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the side length of the pentagon.\nMore formulas can be found at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://xgeometry.com/formulas/pentagon\">https://xgeometry.com/formulas/pentagon</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Construction\">Construction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Construction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Pentagon.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c6/Pentagon.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"359\" height=\"359\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>It is possible to construct a regular pentagon with compass and straightedge:\n</p>\n<ol><li>Draw circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (red).</li>\n<li>Draw diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and construct a perpendicular radius through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Construct the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and label it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> (green).</li>\n<li>Construct the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fecc5bf13d5da857e918aee30205cb0c7018b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEO$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, and label its intersection with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (pink).</li>\n<li>Construct a perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Adjust your compass to length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and mark off points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba021e3606d09b124ca668173a524f11526faadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGHIJ$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is a regular pentagon.</li></ol>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Golden_Ratio\">The Golden Ratio</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: The Golden Ratio\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The pentagon is closely associated with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Golden_Ratio\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Golden Ratio\">Golden Ratio</a>. More specifically, the ratio of a diagonal to an edge is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c2b2e9d216af3f6a5b1536d99a69aa9844a02a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">Polygon</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003122\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 134/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3722/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.508      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.508      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4900:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003122 and revision id 284179. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}